<title>POLAND: POLISH BOURSE CLEARS STALPRODUKT FOR MAIN FLOOR.</title>
<headline>POLISH BOURSE CLEARS STALPRODUKT FOR MAIN FLOOR.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of the Warsaw Stock Exchange (WSE) cleared for trade on the main market shares of steel products maker Stalprodukt SA, it said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It also cleared new share issues of Farm Food, Jutrzenka, Pierwszy Polsko-Amerykanski Bank (PPABank), Mostostal Export and Kredyt Bank.</p>
<p>The board also allowed Elektromontaz Warszawa SA and Polish Life Improvement SA to switch to the primary market from the parallel floor.</p>
<p>It also cleared for parallel market trade Wroclawskie Kopalnie Surowcow Mineralnych SA and Polifarb Debica Fabryka Farb i Lakierow SA as well as the new share issue of Ariel SA.</p>
<p>WSE cleared Brok and Energoaparatura for the third market, which is also called the free market.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
